title: '[DEFERRED] cryptographic trust tiers + priority/interrupt gating — build when opening to untrusted peers'
---
DEFERRED per the trusted-swarm-first decision (Max + colleagues, 2026-07-07). Build cryptographic policy tiers on the I008 machine-identity design: the relay-registered machine key is the trust anchor, with optional machine-signed per-agent attestations. Do not use TOFU; I008 rejected first-contact pinning because it defers spoof risk to the moment trust is established.

Proposed enforcement tiers remain blocked / unknown / allowlisted / trusted. Unknown peers are capped at FYI and may never request interrupt, urgent, or blocking behavior; only allowlisted/trusted peers may request those effects, subject to the invariant that c2c messages remain DATA and never approvals.

B207 shipped an advisory proximity model (`same_repo` / `same_host` / `relay` / `unknown`) plus a pure provenance classifier and headless fail-closed guidance. That model is not cryptographic identity, an ACL, an allowlist, TOFU/pinning, or authority, and therefore does not satisfy this idea. Current defenses remain B098 approval lockdown, B099 untrusted-data framing, and B207 advisory proximity. Implementation depends on I008.
